ement Platform — Overview 
The project is a proposal for the development of a comprehensive Digital Financial Management Platform for UPAM Holdings / UPAM Finance, a microfinance institution.
The goal of the platform is to digitize and centralize the organization's financial and operational processes, making it easier to manage customers, loans, repayments, transactions, accounting, and financial reports from one secure system.
The platform will reduce dependence on manual processes, improve accuracy and transparency, provide better access to financial information, and help management make informed decisions using organized and accessible data.
Main Modules
1. Administrative Dashboard
A centralized dashboard where authorized administrators can monitor the organization's overall activities and view important statistics and financial information.
2. Finance & Accounting
This module will manage the organization's financial activities, including:
•	Income and expenses 
•	Financial transactions 
•	Account balances 
•	Accounting records 
•	Financial monitoring and reporting 
Your suggestion: Add an Activity Log that records important actions performed by users. This will improve accountability, transparency, and security by allowing management to see who performed specific actions and when.
3. Loan Management
This module will manage the loan lifecycle, including:
•	Loan applications 
•	Loan approval 
•	Loan disbursement 
•	Repayments 
•	Loan tracking 
•	Completed loans 
Your suggestions:
•	Add a Search Bar and Filter to quickly find customer loan information and transactions. 
•	Allow staff to search using the customer's name or tracking ID. 
•	Add document upload functionality for customer documents and proof of identity. 
4. Customer Management
A centralized system for managing customer profiles and information. Staff should be able to view a customer's details, loans, repayments, transactions, and uploaded documents in one place.
5. Reporting & Monitoring
The platform will generate reports and provide analytics to help management monitor:
•	Financial performance 
•	Loan performance 
•	Repayments 
•	Customer growth 
•	Transactions 
•	Other important business metrics 
6. Security & User Access
The system should have role-based access control, ensuring that each user only has access to the information and functions relevant to their role.
Your Development Role
Your role is primarily focused on the Frontend/UI development, particularly the Administrative Dashboard interface. The platform is planned around a React-based frontend, while more advanced backend development and database functionality would be handled by the senior developer/backend team.
Your Key Recommendations
Your review of the proposal included four major recommendations:
1.	Activity Log — for accountability in Finance & Accounting. 
2.	Search & Filter — to easily locate loans and transactions by name or tracking ID. 
3.	Customer Document Uploads — to store and manage identity and other relevant documents. 
4.	Phased Development — to make the project easier to develop, test, launch, and expand over time. 
Overall Goal
To create a secure, centralized, and efficient digital financial management system that enables UPAM Finance to manage its customers, loans, financial transactions, accounting operations, and reporting processes more effectively.
